-- title:
--   Points in both component closures are crossing points
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0$ be a nonzero natural number and $q$ a prime with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN` for level $(N_0,q)$. Let $O$ be a local commutative ring together with a ring homomorphism $\rho_O \colon \mathbb{R}_q \to O$ from the base ring `DRLevel.R q`, and assume that the maximal ideal of $O$ is the principal ideal generated by the image of $q$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_O = (q)$. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism, so that $\kappa$ becomes an $\mathbb{R}_q$-algebra through the composite. Write $\mathfrak X_O =$ `DRLevel.XO ρO` for the base change of the model along $\rho_O$, and $b =$ `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ` for the induced morphism from the fibre over the composite $\mathbb{R}_q \to \kappa$ to $\mathfrak X_O$ (the pullback map built from the identity on the model and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $O \to \kappa$). Let $x$ be a point of the underlying space of $\mathfrak X_O$ lying both in the closure of the set-theoretic image of the morphism `𝔛.comp κ _ 0` followed by $b$, and in the closure of the image of `𝔛.comp κ _ 1` followed by $b$. Then there is a point $n$ of the pullback of the two component morphisms `𝔛.comp κ _ 0` and `𝔛.comp κ _ 1` with $x = \mathfrak X.\mathrm{crossingPt}(\rho_O, \mathrm{to}\kappa)(n)$, that is, $x$ is the image of $n$ under the first projection of that pullback, followed by `𝔛.comp κ _ 0` and then by $b$.
--
--   In the Deligne–Rapoport picture of the model of $X_0(N_0q)$ over the base at $q$, the special fibre consists of two components meeting at the supersingular points; the statement says that a point of the base-changed model lying in the closures of the images of both components must be one of the crossing points, with no further hypothesis on $x$. It is used in the level-$(N_0,q)$ analysis of the special fibre, by [`V3AsmLevel.comp_prod`](thm.html#V3AsmLevel.comp_prod), [`V3AsmLevel.edgePt_exhaust`](thm.html#V3AsmLevel.edgePt_exhaust) and [`V3AsmLevel.edgePt_transversal`](thm.html#V3AsmLevel.edgePt_transversal).
